          "id": "sec-1-7",
          "secNumber": "1.7",
          "heading": "Engineering Audit, Diagnostic Reasoning & Assessment: Conservation Framework, Microscopic Control Volumes and Flux Laws",
          "content": "# Unit 1 Assessment \u2014 Conservation framework\n\n1. Explain the physical principle supporting Defining a control volume and state all assumptions in dM/dt = \u03a3 m\u0307_in \u2212 \u03a3 m\u0307_out + m\u0307_generated.\n2. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of dM/dt = \u03a3 m\u0307_in \u2212 \u03a3 m\u0307_out + m\u0307_generated; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n3. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Defining a control volume.\n4. Explain the physical principle supporting Local continuity equation and state all assumptions in \u2202\u03c1/\u2202t + \u2207\u00b7(\u03c1u) = 0.\n5. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of \u2202\u03c1/\u2202t + \u2207\u00b7(\u03c1u) = 0; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n6. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Local continuity equation.\n7. Explain the physical principle supporting Momentum conservation and state all assumptions in d/dt \u222bCV \u03c1u dV = \u2212\u222eCS \u03c1u(u\u00b7n)dA + \u03a3F.\n8. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of d/dt \u222bCV \u03c1u dV = \u2212\u222eCS \u03c1u(u\u00b7n)dA + \u03a3F; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n9. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Momentum conservation.\n10. Explain the physical principle supporting Energy and species conservation and state all assumptions in \u2202(\u03c1c)/\u2202t + \u2207\u00b7(\u03c1uc) = \u2212\u2207\u00b7J + r.\n11. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of \u2202(\u03c1c)/\u2202t + \u2207\u00b7(\u03c1uc) = \u2212\u2207\u00b7J + r; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n12. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Energy and species conservation."
