          "heading": "Process Simulation & Industrial Design Case: Momentum Transport, Shell Balances and Differential Navier-Stokes",
          "content": "# Applied Project 2 \u2014 Momentum transport\n\nDevelop an engineering model. Supply geometry, conservation equations, units, two operating points, simulation plots, uncertainty, and a validation plan.\n\n## Detailed project brief\n\nStudy a proposed laboratory pipe carrying a 1000 kg/m\u00b3 liquid of viscosity 0.003 Pa\u00b7s through 6 m of 25 mm internal diameter. Compare mean speeds of 0.1, 0.4 and 1.0 m/s. Calculate Reynolds number at each operating point and decide which friction-factor assumptions can be defended. Estimate pressure loss using a declared Darcy convention, and compute hydraulic power from \u0394pQ. Next, investigate a smooth-pipe diameter increase and record effects on velocity and pump demand when volumetric throughput\u2014not speed\u2014is held fixed. Explain why it is incorrect to reuse laminar Poiseuille flow above its Reynolds applicability range. Discuss how upstream elbows, temperature variation and wall roughness could affect the trial."
