          "heading": "Engineering Audit, Diagnostic Reasoning & Assessment: Momentum Transport, Shell Balances and Differential Navier-Stokes",
          "content": "# Unit 2 Assessment \u2014 Momentum transport\n\n1. Explain the physical principle supporting Viscosity and Newtonian stress and state all assumptions in \u03c4_xy = \u03bc \u2202u/\u2202y.\n2. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of \u03c4_xy = \u03bc \u2202u/\u2202y; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n3. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Viscosity and Newtonian stress.\n4. Explain the physical principle supporting Plane Couette and Poiseuille flow and state all assumptions in u(y) = Uy/h \u2212 (1/2\u03bc)(dp/dx)y(h\u2212y).\n5. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of u(y) = Uy/h \u2212 (1/2\u03bc)(dp/dx)y(h\u2212y); what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n6. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Plane Couette and Poiseuille flow.\n7. Explain the physical principle supporting Laminar pipe flow and state all assumptions in Q = \u03c0R\u2074\u0394p/(8\u03bcL).\n8. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of Q = \u03c0R\u2074\u0394p/(8\u03bcL); what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n9. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Laminar pipe flow.\n10. Explain the physical principle supporting Reynolds number and friction and state all assumptions in Re = \u03c1VD/\u03bc; \u0394p = f(L/D)\u03c1V\u00b2/2.\n11. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of Re = \u03c1VD/\u03bc; \u0394p = f(L/D)\u03c1V\u00b2/2; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n12. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Reynolds number and friction."
