          "id": "sec-5-6",
          "secNumber": "5.6",
          "heading": "Process Simulation & Industrial Design Case: Convective Heat Transfer, Dimensionless Numbers and Thermal Boundary Layers",
          "content": "# Applied Project 5 \u2014 Boundary layers\n\nDevelop an engineering model. Supply geometry, conservation equations, units, two operating points, simulation plots, uncertainty, and a validation plan.\n\n## Detailed project brief\n\nSet up a thermal boundary-layer experiment using a smooth heated plate in airflow. Compare mean speeds of 1.0 and 3.0 m/s with representative kinematic viscosity of 1.6\u00d710\u207b\u2075 m\u00b2/s. At two downstream positions, calculate local Reynolds numbers and laminar-layer thickness estimates, then state why the leading-edge result is only an asymptotic approximation. Introduce two working fluids with contrasting Prandtl numbers and estimate how their thermal layers scale relative to momentum layers. Convert an independently measured heat-transfer coefficient into Nusselt number using a clearly stated characteristic length. Propose temperature and velocity measurements that would identify early transition or unwanted natural convection."
