          "id": "sec-6-6",
          "secNumber": "6.6",
          "heading": "Process Simulation & Industrial Design Case: Molecular Mass Diffusion, Fickian Shell Balances and Species Fluxes",
          "content": "# Applied Project 6 \u2014 Multidimensional models\n\nDevelop an engineering model. Supply geometry, conservation equations, units, two operating points, simulation plots, uncertainty, and a validation plan.\n\n## Detailed project brief\n\nAssess a spherical insulation shell around a small heated reactor sensor. Choose an inner radius of 3 cm, outer radius of 12 cm, conductivity 0.25 W/(m K), and inner/outer face temperatures of 80 and 20 \u00b0C. Calculate thermal resistance and steady heat rate from the spherical formula, then compare a planar approximation based on the inner area. Develop a three-cell radial finite-volume sketch showing where face areas enter discrete fluxes. Verify that each steady cell passes the same heat rate. Finally, impose an external convection boundary instead of prescribed outer temperature and explain which additional equation becomes necessary. Present a plot of temperature versus radius and reciprocal radius to reveal the correct functional dependence."
