          "heading": "Engineering Audit, Diagnostic Reasoning & Assessment: Molecular Mass Diffusion, Fickian Shell Balances and Species Fluxes",
          "content": "# Unit 6 Assessment \u2014 Multidimensional models\n\n1. Explain the physical principle supporting Radial heat flow in cylinders and state all assumptions in q = 2\u03c0kL\u0394T/ln(r_o/r_i).\n2. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of q = 2\u03c0kL\u0394T/ln(r_o/r_i); what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n3. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Radial heat flow in cylinders.\n4. Explain the physical principle supporting Radial transport through spheres and state all assumptions in q = 4\u03c0k\u0394T/(1/r_i \u2212 1/r_o).\n5. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of q = 4\u03c0k\u0394T/(1/r_i \u2212 1/r_o); what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n6. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Radial transport through spheres.\n7. Explain the physical principle supporting Two-dimensional conduction and state all assumptions in \u2202\u00b2T/\u2202x\u00b2+\u2202\u00b2T/\u2202y\u00b2=0.\n8. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of \u2202\u00b2T/\u2202x\u00b2+\u2202\u00b2T/\u2202y\u00b2=0; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n9. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Two-dimensional conduction.\n10. Explain the physical principle supporting Transient PDEs and boundary conditions and state all assumptions in \u2202T/\u2202t = \u03b1\u2207\u00b2T.\n11. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of \u2202T/\u2202t = \u03b1\u2207\u00b2T; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n12. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Transient PDEs and boundary conditions."
