          "id": "sec-8-6",
          "secNumber": "8.6",
          "heading": "Process Simulation & Industrial Design Case: Macroscopic Transport Balances, Interphase Transport and Universal Analogies",
          "content": "# Applied Project 8 \u2014 Computational methods\n\nDevelop an engineering model. Supply geometry, conservation equations, units, two operating points, simulation plots, uncertainty, and a validation plan.\n\n## Detailed project brief\n\nBuild a transparent numerical benchmark for diffusion of a one-dimensional tracer pulse. Choose diffusivity D=10\u207b\u2074 m\u00b2/s, spacing \u0394x=1 cm and two time steps: 0.1 and 0.8 s. Evaluate the discrete Fourier number for each, identify the stable and unstable cases under FTCS assumptions, and compare predicted profiles after equal physical times. With zero-flux walls, monitor discrete total inventory; with zero-concentration walls, explain why inventory may decrease. Refine the grid while adjusting the time step to preserve stability. Report the peak concentration, integrated inventory and profile error against a Gaussian analytical reference before boundaries materially affect the pulse. Distinguish code verification from eventual laboratory validation."
