          "id": "sec-8-7",
          "secNumber": "8.7",
          "heading": "Engineering Audit, Diagnostic Reasoning & Assessment: Macroscopic Transport Balances, Interphase Transport and Universal Analogies",
          "content": "# Unit 8 Assessment \u2014 Computational methods\n\n1. Explain the physical principle supporting Scaling and nondimensionalization and state all assumptions in Pe = UL/D; Fo = Dt/L\u00b2.\n2. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of Pe = UL/D; Fo = Dt/L\u00b2; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n3. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Scaling and nondimensionalization.\n4. Explain the physical principle supporting Explicit diffusion discretization and state all assumptions in c_i\u207f\u207a\u00b9 = c_i\u207f + Fo(c_i\u208b\u2081\u207f\u22122c_i\u207f+c_i\u208a\u2081\u207f).\n5. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of c_i\u207f\u207a\u00b9 = c_i\u207f + Fo(c_i\u208b\u2081\u207f\u22122c_i\u207f+c_i\u208a\u2081\u207f); what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n6. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Explicit diffusion discretization.\n7. Explain the physical principle supporting Finite-volume conservation and state all assumptions in (M_i\u207f\u207a\u00b9\u2212M_i\u207f)/\u0394t = F_{i\u22121/2}\u2212F_{i+1/2}+S_i.\n8. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of (M_i\u207f\u207a\u00b9\u2212M_i\u207f)/\u0394t = F_{i\u22121/2}\u2212F_{i+1/2}+S_i; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n9. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Finite-volume conservation.\n10. Explain the physical principle supporting Mesh convergence and validation and state all assumptions in e_h = |Q_h\u2212Q_ref|; convergence requires systematic reduction.\n11. Derive a dimensionless or limiting-form check of e_h = |Q_h\u2212Q_ref|; convergence requires systematic reduction; what happens when the driving gradient tends to zero?\n12. Design an experiment to distinguish a boundary-condition error from an incorrect material coefficient for Mesh convergence and validation."
